1
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:11,380
A road sign in the UK says: Edinburgh, 45 miles.

2
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:15,270
But the car's trip computer is set to kilometres.

3
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:18,500
Is a mile longer or shorter than a kilometre?

4
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:22,780
A useful fact is that 5 miles is about 8 kilometres.

5
00:00:22,830 --> 00:00:25,180
How many kilometres is 45 miles?

6
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:28,970
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,490
45 miles is 9 lots of 5 miles.

8
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:36,720
So it is 9 lots of 8 kilometres, which is 72 kilometres.

9
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:42,770
Remember: 8 fifths of 30 is 30 divided by 5, times 8, which is 48.

10
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:48,900
And 5 eighths of 40 is 40 divided by 8, times 5, which is 25.

11
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:51,390
A mile is longer than a kilometre.

12
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,140
5 miles is about 8 kilometres.

13
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:58,650
To change miles to kilometres, divide by 5 and multiply by 8.

14
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:03,710
To change kilometres to miles, divide by 8 and multiply by 5.

15
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:04,450
Your turn.

16
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,790
How many kilometres is 15 miles?

17
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:10,160
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:10,210 --> 00:01:15,810
15 divided by 5 is 3, and 3 times 8 is 24 kilometres.

19
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:22,700
For the same distance, the number of kilometres is always bigger, about 1.6 times the miles.

20
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:29,170
Speeds convert the same way: 50 miles per hour is about 80 kilometres per hour.

21
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,630
Here is the method.

22
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:35,170
Step 1: remember that 5 miles is about 8 kilometres.

23
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:40,380
Step 2: miles to kilometres, divide by 5, then multiply by 8.

24
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:45,650
Step 3: kilometres to miles, divide by 8, then multiply by 5.

25
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,670
Step 4: check.

26
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:50,350
The kilometres should be the bigger number.

27
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,620
Convert 120 kilometres to miles.

28
00:01:53,670 --> 00:01:55,970
120 divided by 8 is 15.

29
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,870
15 times 5 is 75 miles.

30
00:01:58,920 --> 00:01:59,650
Your turn.

31
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,220
How many miles is 200 kilometres?

32
00:02:02,270 --> 00:02:05,330
Pause and work it out.

33
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:08,060
200 divided by 8 is 25.

34
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:11,450
25 times 5 is 125 miles.

35
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,510
Which is further: 30 miles, or 45 kilometres?

36
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:21,010
30 miles is 30 divided by 5, times 8, which is 48 kilometres.

37
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:25,440
48 is more than 45, so 30 miles is further.

38
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:28,630
A speed limit is 70 miles per hour.

39
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:35,110
70 divided by 5 is 14, and 14 times 8 is 112 kilometres per hour.

40
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:40,100
For numbers that are not multiples of 5, multiply by 1.6.

41
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:45,100
13 miles is 13 times 1.6, which is 20.8 kilometres.

42
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,860
Ola converts 40 miles to kilometres.

43
00:02:47,910 --> 00:02:49,940
Which line is wrong?

44
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:51,050
Line 1 is wrong.

45
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:53,900
The kilometres must be the bigger number.

46
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:56,390
She used the wrong fraction.

47
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:00,220
40 times 8 fifths is 64 kilometres.

48
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:03,290
A marathon is about 26.2 miles long.

49
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:08,330
Using 1.6 kilometres per mile, that is about 42 kilometres.

50
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:12,550
The official distance is 42.195 kilometres.

51
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,850
One last question.

52
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:16,660
Which is longer: 1 mile or 1 kilometre?

53
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:20,000
Pause the video and choose.

54
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:21,420
1 mile is longer.

55
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:24,220
It is about 1.6 kilometres.

56
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:28,010
To remember: 5 miles is about 8 kilometres.

57
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:30,720
Miles to kilometres, times 8 fifths.

58
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:34,050
Kilometres to miles, times 5 eighths.

59
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,880
Kilometres are about 1.6 times the miles.

60
00:03:37,930 --> 00:03:40,620
Speeds convert in the same way.

61
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:46,030
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.1 on Camday.
